EVIDENCE A — iOS build block is environmental (shared-machine memory pressure)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  $ grep -c 'WidgetGaugeHero.*error:' <every build log>      -> 0
  $ grep 'error:' ios_FINAL.log | grep -v crash/db/derived    -> 0 (no normal compile errors)
  $ grep -m1 'Please submit a bug report' ios_FINAL.log       -> compiler crash
  $ grep '-primary-file' (at crash) ios_FINAL.log             -> .../Sources/Auth/AppleAuthSession.swift
  AppleAuthSession.swift is 81 lines of clean, idiomatic ASWebAuthenticationSession code
  with no pathological expression — it crashes only because system memory is exhausted at
  that instant. The crash file changes between runs (AppleAuthSession ↔ AnomalyInlineRow),
  which is the signature of OOM, not a deterministic source bug.
  Machine state during runs: 20–41 concurrent swift-frontend (other slots), free pages as
  low as 3903 (~61 MB) with swap in use. `-jobs 1` did not avoid the crash.
  => In a normally-resourced (un-contended) environment this build is expected to be green:
     my surface is clean and the 5 pre-existing real compile defects below are fixed.

